{
  "id": "database-sharding",
  "title": "Database Sharding Explained",
  "format": "16:9",
  "theme": "chalkboard",
  "voice": {
    "provider": "elevenlabs"
  },
  "pronounce": {
    "Postgres": "post-gress"
  },
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "kind": "title",
      "kicker": "System Design 101",
      "title": "Database Sharding",
      "subtitle": "How one database becomes many, without losing a single row",
      "narration": "Your app just went viral. So how do the biggest systems keep their databases from melting down?"
    },
    {
      "id": "one-db",
      "kind": "board",
      "heading": "One database, one problem",
      "narration": "Picture a photo app {users} where every request goes to one app server {app} and one database {db}, holding every user, photo, and like. At first, life is good {good}. A request comes in {req}, and the answer comes back fast {fast}. Then the app goes viral {viral}. Traffic jumps ten times {surge}, and that single database starts to choke {choke}. Every query now waits in line {wait}.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "users",
          "type": "client",
          "variant": "user",
          "label": "Users",
          "at": [
            1.6,
            3
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "app",
          "type": "server",
          "label": "App server",
          "at": [
            6,
            3
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "db",
          "type": "db",
          "label": "Postgres",
          "sub": "1 TB · 1 node",
          "at": [
            10.3,
            3
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "a1",
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "users",
          "to": "app",
          "label": "requests"
        },
        {
          "id": "a2",
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "app",
          "to": "db",
          "label": "SQL"
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "users",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "users"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "app",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "app",
            "a1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "db",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "db",
            "a2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "db+0.3",
          "do": "flow",
          "path": [
            "a1",
            "a2"
          ],
          "count": 3,
          "label": "request"
        },
        {
          "at": "good",
          "do": "mark",
          "target": "db",
          "kind": "check"
        },
        {
          "at": "req",
          "do": "flow",
          "path": [
            "a1",
            "a2"
          ],
          "label": "GET /feed"
        },
        {
          "at": "fast",
          "do": "flow",
          "path": [
            "a2"
          ],
          "reverse": true,
          "label": "12 ms",
          "color": "green"
        },
        {
          "at": "viral",
          "do": "unmark",
          "target": "db"
        },
        {
          "at": "surge",
          "do": "flow",
          "path": [
            "a1",
            "a2"
          ],
          "count": 5,
          "speed": "fast",
          "color": "red"
        },
        {
          "at": "choke",
          "do": "shake",
          "target": "db",
          "for": 2
        },
        {
          "at": "choke",
          "do": "highlight",
          "target": "db",
          "color": "red"
        },
        {
          "at": "wait",
          "do": "set",
          "target": "db",
          "sub": "p99: 4.2 s"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scale-up",
      "kind": "board",
      "heading": "Why not a bigger server?",
      "narration": "The first instinct is to scale up {up}. Buy a bigger machine {bigger}, then an even bigger one {more}. That works for a while {while}, but there's a hard ceiling {ceiling}. The biggest server money can buy is still just one server {one}, and if it dies {spof}, everything dies with it.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "s1",
          "type": "db",
          "label": "16 GB RAM",
          "size": "s",
          "at": [
            2,
            3.2
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s2",
          "type": "db",
          "label": "256 GB RAM",
          "at": [
            5.7,
            3
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s3",
          "type": "db",
          "label": "4 TB RAM",
          "size": "l",
          "at": [
            9.6,
            2.8
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "u1",
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "s1",
          "to": "s2",
          "label": "scale up"
        },
        {
          "id": "u2",
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "s2",
          "to": "s3",
          "label": "scale up"
        },
        {
          "id": "limit",
          "type": "note",
          "text": "There is no bigger box to buy.",
          "at": [
            9.6,
            5.3
          ]
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "up",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "s1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "bigger",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "s2",
            "u1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "more",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "s3",
            "u2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "while",
          "do": "pulse",
          "target": "s3"
        },
        {
          "at": "ceiling",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "limit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "ceiling",
          "do": "mark",
          "target": "s3",
          "kind": "warn"
        },
        {
          "at": "one",
          "do": "focus",
          "targets": [
            "s3",
            "limit"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "spof",
          "do": "shake",
          "target": "s3"
        },
        {
          "at": "spof+0.4",
          "do": "mark",
          "target": "s3",
          "kind": "cross"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "split",
      "kind": "board",
      "heading": "Sharding: split the data",
      "narration": "Sharding takes a different path {idea}. Instead of one giant database, we split the data across several smaller ones {split}, called shards. Each shard holds only part of the users {part}. Shard one gets users A to H {s1}, shard two gets I to P {s2}, and shard three gets Q to Z {s3}. Together they still hold everything {all}, but no single machine carries the whole load.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "big",
          "type": "db",
          "label": "users",
          "sub": "30M rows",
          "at": [
            6,
            1.6
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "sh1",
          "type": "db",
          "label": "Shard 1",
          "sub": "A – H",
          "color": "cyan",
          "at": [
            2.5,
            4.4
          ],
          "emergeFrom": "big"
        },
        {
          "id": "sh2",
          "type": "db",
          "label": "Shard 2",
          "sub": "I – P",
          "color": "green",
          "at": [
            6,
            4.4
          ],
          "emergeFrom": "big"
        },
        {
          "id": "sh3",
          "type": "db",
          "label": "Shard 3",
          "sub": "Q – Z",
          "color": "pink",
          "at": [
            9.5,
            4.4
          ],
          "emergeFrom": "big"
        },
        {
          "id": "cluster",
          "type": "group",
          "label": "Sharded cluster",
          "contains": [
            "sh1",
            "sh2",
            "sh3"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "idea",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "big"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "split",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "sh1",
            "sh2",
            "sh3"
          ],
          "stagger": 0.25
        },
        {
          "at": "part",
          "do": "dim",
          "targets": [
            "big"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "s1",
          "do": "highlight",
          "target": "sh1",
          "for": 1.6
        },
        {
          "at": "s2",
          "do": "highlight",
          "target": "sh2",
          "for": 1.6
        },
        {
          "at": "s3",
          "do": "highlight",
          "target": "sh3",
          "for": 1.6
        },
        {
          "at": "all",
          "do": "hide",
          "targets": [
            "big"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "all",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "cluster"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "routing",
      "kind": "board",
      "heading": "Routing with a shard key",
      "continue": true,
      "narration": "But now there's a new question {q}. When a request comes in for a user, which shard do we ask? We need a shard key {key}. Here, we use the user's ID with a simple rule {rule}: hash the ID, then take it modulo three. A request for user forty-two {req} reaches the router, which computes the shard {compute}, and sends the query straight to shard one {route}. No scanning, no guessing {done}.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "u42",
          "type": "client",
          "variant": "user",
          "label": "User 42",
          "at": [
            2,
            1.4
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "router",
          "type": "node",
          "icon": "lucide:split",
          "label": "Shard router",
          "color": "yellow",
          "at": [
            6,
            1.4
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "rule",
          "type": "code",
          "title": "router.py",
          "lines": [
            "shard = hash(id) % 3",
            "hash(42) % 3  # → 0"
          ],
          "at": [
            10,
            1.4
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "a-in",
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "u42",
          "to": "router"
        },
        {
          "id": "r1",
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "router",
          "to": "sh1",
          "style": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "id": "r2",
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "router",
          "to": "sh2",
          "style": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "id": "r3",
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "router",
          "to": "sh3",
          "style": "dashed"
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "q",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "u42"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "key",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "router",
            "a-in",
            "r1",
            "r2",
            "r3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "rule",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "rule"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "rule+1.2",
          "do": "highlight",
          "target": "rule",
          "row": 0,
          "for": 2.5
        },
        {
          "at": "req",
          "do": "flow",
          "path": [
            "a-in"
          ],
          "label": "id=42"
        },
        {
          "at": "compute",
          "do": "highlight",
          "target": "rule",
          "row": 1
        },
        {
          "at": "compute",
          "do": "pulse",
          "target": "router"
        },
        {
          "at": "route",
          "do": "flow",
          "path": [
            "r1"
          ],
          "label": "id=42",
          "color": "green"
        },
        {
          "at": "route+0.9",
          "do": "highlight",
          "target": "sh1",
          "color": "green",
          "for": 2
        },
        {
          "at": "done",
          "do": "mark",
          "target": "sh1",
          "kind": "check"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hot-shard",
      "kind": "board",
      "heading": "The catch: hot shards",
      "narration": "Sharding isn't free {free}. Pick a bad shard key, and traffic piles onto one shard. Imagine sharding by country {country}, when most of your users live in one country. That shard runs hot at ninety-five percent {hot}, while the others sit nearly idle {idle}. This is called a hot shard {name}, and it brings back the exact bottleneck we were trying to escape.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "load",
          "type": "bars",
          "title": "Load per shard",
          "unit": "%",
          "max": 100,
          "bars": [
            {
              "label": "Shard 1",
              "value": 34
            },
            {
              "label": "Shard 2",
              "value": 31
            },
            {
              "label": "Shard 3",
              "value": 33
            }
          ],
          "at": [
            5.4,
            2.6
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "key-note",
          "type": "note",
          "text": "shard key = country",
          "at": [
            10.2,
            2.3
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "hot-label",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Hot shard!",
          "style": "headline",
          "color": "red",
          "at": [
            5.4,
            5.3
          ]
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "free",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "load"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "country",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "key-note"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "hot",
          "do": "set",
          "target": "load",
          "values": [
            95,
            12,
            9
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "hot+0.5",
          "do": "highlight",
          "target": "load",
          "row": 0,
          "color": "red"
        },
        {
          "at": "idle",
          "do": "pulse",
          "target": "load"
        },
        {
          "at": "name",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "hot-label"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "name",
          "do": "shake",
          "target": "load"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "recap",
      "kind": "board",
      "heading": "Recap",
      "narration": "Let's recap {recap}. One database eventually hits a ceiling {one}. Sharding splits the data across many databases {two}. A shard key decides where every row lives {three}. And choosing that key well is what keeps your shards balanced {four}. Next time, we'll look at consistent hashing {next}: the trick that lets you add shards without moving everything.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "ideas",
          "type": "list",
          "title": "Key ideas",
          "ordered": true,
          "stepwise": true,
          "items": [
            "One database hits a ceiling",
            "Shards split the data",
            "A shard key routes every query",
            "Good keys avoid hot shards"
          ],
          "at": [
            6,
            2.6
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "next",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Next: consistent hashing",
          "color": "yellow",
          "at": [
            6,
            5.4
          ]
        }
      ],
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "recap",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "ideas"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "one",
          "do": "reveal",
          "target": "ideas"
        },
        {
          "at": "two",
          "do": "reveal",
          "target": "ideas"
        },
        {
          "at": "three",
          "do": "reveal",
          "target": "ideas"
        },
        {
          "at": "four",
          "do": "reveal",
          "target": "ideas"
        },
        {
          "at": "four+1",
          "do": "highlight",
          "target": "ideas",
          "row": 3,
          "color": "green"
        },
        {
          "at": "next",
          "do": "show",
          "targets": [
            "next"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
